WEBVTT

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:29.590
It was here in Fukuhara that I found you.

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:34.550
Koremori...

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:52.190
THE HEIKE STORY

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:11.230
Episode 10

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:17.910
Lord Koremori's head was not paraded.

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:22.290
It appears that he was not present
at Ichinotani, due to illness.

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:23.620
So then...

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:25.330
He is in Yashima.

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:28.170
Is this "Yashima" far from the capital?

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:31.630
Will Father recover from his illness?

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:34.090
I wish he would come back for us soon.

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:41.140
A letter arrived from Shigehira.

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:46.230
I heard he was captured while
escaping from Ichinotani. He's alive?!

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:51.190
It seems he was captured
and paraded through the city.

00:02:52.570 --> 00:02:53.990
How awful.

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:58.200
What did Shigehira write?

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:01.160
He asks us to return the Sacred Treasures.

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:06.710
He says that is Emperor
Go-Shirakawa's wish.

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:13.210
Munemori,

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:18.010
if we send the Treasures to the capital,
will Shigehira be returned?

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:22.470
Mother, I understand exactly
how you feel, but...

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:27.810
Even if we return the Treasures,
Shigehira may not be returned.

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:29.310
But Tomomori--

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:31.270
Mother.

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:36.280
Let us protect Emperor Antoku here.

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:39.950
Where the Emperor is becomes the capital.

00:03:43.370 --> 00:03:45.910
They decided not to return
the Sacred Treasures.

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:50.790
Then what will become of Lord Shigehira?

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:53.920
He is to be sent to Kamakura.

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:55.460
I see.

00:03:55.460 --> 00:04:00.140
As things stand, the war will resume.
The Genji--Yoshitsune will attack.

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:03.640
I am scared.

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:05.140
You still...

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:10.770
Brother, you've been a scaredy-cat
since we were kids...

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:15.860
I know I will fall...

00:04:18.530 --> 00:04:20.030
...fall straight into hell.

00:04:21.910 --> 00:04:23.660
It is all over.

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:25.450
The Heike will end.

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:29.830
When Kiyotsune jumped...

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:32.040
...this must have been how he felt.

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:37.340
I must do something so it does not end.

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:40.010
Try to think of a plan, too, Brother.

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:46.890
I present Lord Taira no Shigehira.

00:04:46.890 --> 00:04:49.350
The one who burned Nara?

00:04:55.570 --> 00:05:00.240
The fires we set to see in the dark
of night were fanned by the wind...

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:05.700
As I was in command at the time,

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:06.910
that sin was...

00:05:06.910 --> 00:05:11.080
...mine, and mine alone.

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:15.420
That I have been captured
and dishonored in this fashion

00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:17.300
is but karmic retribution.

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:22.470
It is my just desert for
the battle and conflict,

00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:26.930
for destroying others and
attempting to save only myself.

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:30.730
I have been made well aware of that.

00:05:40.490 --> 00:05:42.700
What concerns you so?

00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:45.200
The tree peony.

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:48.330
Do you mean Lord Shigehira?

00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:52.040
Indeed, I had heard him
likened to the tree peony.

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:54.830
The man was truly like that flower.

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:58.880
Do you hope to spare him?

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:04.880
You are here now because
Lord Kiyomori spared your life.

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:08.720
And you are about to end the Heike.

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:14.140
If you were to spare Lord Shigehira,
nay, any of the Taira clan...

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:18.570
...one will rise... to end the Genji?

00:06:18.570 --> 00:06:25.360
Pity might move many to serve a truly
genteel flower raised in the capital.

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:47.550
Lord Koremori has vanished?

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:50.930
He doesn't mean to save only
his own skin, does he?

00:06:55.690 --> 00:06:56.940
Write to him!

00:06:56.940 --> 00:06:58.980
And write what, Sukemori?

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:01.190
Write a letter to Emperor Go-Shirakawa.

00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:05.280
Lady Tokuko, you were on
good terms with His Majesty.

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:07.280
Yes, and write what exactly?

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:09.700
Implore him to spare us!

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:14.250
If he decrees that the Genji
no longer need to attack the Heike...

00:07:14.250 --> 00:07:15.370
Lady Tokuko!

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:22.670
I am afraid he is the same as my father.

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:26.470
He does not easily forgive
those who threatened him.

00:07:26.470 --> 00:07:28.510
Then we just wait for the end--

00:07:28.510 --> 00:07:29.760
I will protect him.

00:07:36.310 --> 00:07:37.940
Whatever befalls <i>us</i>...

00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:42.110
...I shall at least protect <i>the emperor</i>.

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:56.120
This seems like neither a dream
nor reality, Lord Koremori.

00:07:56.120 --> 00:08:00.170
Why did you run away from Yashima?

00:08:00.170 --> 00:08:01.840
I wish to become a monk.

00:08:03.340 --> 00:08:06.510
Do you harbor no attachments to the world?

00:08:06.510 --> 00:08:10.890
I considered seeing my wife
and children one last time.

00:08:10.890 --> 00:08:14.720
But if I enter the capital,
I may be taken prisoner.

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:17.980
And after you take your vows?

00:08:17.980 --> 00:08:20.850
I no longer see any merit to living.

00:08:23.860 --> 00:08:25.940
I want to put an end to it.

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:30.240
The running, the fear, the battles...

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:33.280
I-Is...

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:37.910
Is that a shameful and cowardly thing?

00:08:37.910 --> 00:08:42.880
I, too, came here to escape.

00:08:42.880 --> 00:08:49.220
I became a monk to escape the pain of
being separated from the woman I loved.

00:08:49.220 --> 00:08:53.720
Some may think that too trivial a reason.

00:08:53.720 --> 00:09:00.190
However, the suffering one person can
endure may be unbearable for another.

00:09:00.190 --> 00:09:04.310
Numerous misfortunes have
befallen you, Lord Koremori.

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:06.320
How you must have suffered...

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:54.950
Koremori!

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:04.170
Biwa!

00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:11.720
Biwa! You're okay!

00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:20.100
You could see this, couldn't you.

00:10:20.100 --> 00:10:21.220
Koremori,

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:23.850
I know I can't change this,

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:27.980
but couldn't you change your name
and live quietly somewhere?

00:10:36.070 --> 00:10:37.530
I have to go now.

00:10:41.790 --> 00:10:46.460
Your eyes are like Father's.
They're beautiful.

00:10:46.460 --> 00:10:48.540
Koremori,

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:51.300
I shall tell your story, too.

00:10:51.300 --> 00:10:53.420
My story?

00:10:53.420 --> 00:10:57.550
All I ever did was run away.

00:10:57.550 --> 00:11:03.180
I know you very well.
I want to appreciate you.

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:06.600
Then maybe my life had some merit.

00:11:17.660 --> 00:11:25.750
<i>Namu Amida Bu... Namu Amida Bu...</i>

00:11:41.550 --> 00:11:47.310
<i>Namu Amida Bu... Namu Amida Bu...</i>

00:11:47.310 --> 00:11:53.820
<i>Namu Amida Bu... Namu Amida Bu...</i>

00:11:55.690 --> 00:11:59.410
<i>Namu Amida Bu...</i>

00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:15.960
Koremori...

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:20.010
You were a scaredy-cat to the end.

00:12:23.850 --> 00:12:26.730
We're dancing before Emperor Go-Shirakawa?

00:12:26.730 --> 00:12:27.640
That's right.

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:31.350
Maybe a beautiful nobleman
will fall in love with one of us!

00:12:31.350 --> 00:12:35.610
Well, don't get too distracted.
Focus on your dancing.

00:12:35.610 --> 00:12:36.690
Okay!

00:12:41.660 --> 00:12:43.200
Your Majesty.

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:45.160
Lord Yoshitsune is here.

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:49.660
That darn Sukemori
is begging for his life.

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:51.580
Use this to light firewood.

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:53.080
As you wish.

00:12:53.080 --> 00:12:55.630
Why, Lord Yoshitsune!

00:12:55.630 --> 00:13:01.300
I am truly grateful for your invitation
to the cherry blossom banquet today.

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:03.300
How are things in the capital?

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:07.640
There is no particular unrest.
Everyone is greeting a mild spring.

00:13:09.060 --> 00:13:12.150
I am glad I entrusted the capital to you.

00:13:12.150 --> 00:13:16.020
You don't deploy <i>kaburo</i>
like the Heike did,

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:19.490
nor do you commit violence like Yoshinaka.

00:13:19.490 --> 00:13:26.490
It is my duty to protect the city in which
you and Emperor Go-Toba reside.

00:13:28.580 --> 00:13:31.160
Enjoy yourself today.

00:14:10.450 --> 00:14:13.920
Lord Sukemori, did you need something?

00:14:13.920 --> 00:14:16.630
Did anything arrive from the capital?

00:14:16.630 --> 00:14:18.040
Such as?

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:20.920
A letter from Emperor Go-Shirakawa.

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:22.510
None has arrived.

00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:26.890
Any others?

00:14:26.890 --> 00:14:28.470
Other what?

00:14:28.470 --> 00:14:31.680
Did any other letters arrive?

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:33.560
You're not very attentive.

00:14:33.560 --> 00:14:38.520
That must be why you didn't stop
Koremori from jumping into the ocean.

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:41.190
You just shamelessly came back here.

00:14:41.190 --> 00:14:43.740
Whereas the others all jum--

00:14:47.990 --> 00:14:50.200
Nevermind. You can leave now.

00:14:57.670 --> 00:14:59.790
I am terribly sorry.

00:15:05.340 --> 00:15:10.810
♪  Was I born to have fun? ♪

00:15:10.810 --> 00:15:15.310
♪  Was I born to play games? ♪

00:15:18.860 --> 00:15:23.900
-- ♪ When I hear the shouts of--
-- ♪ When I hear the shouts of children playing, ♪

00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:26.070
♪  then even I ♪

00:15:26.070 --> 00:15:28.450
♪ am stirred. ♪

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:33.330
Biwa?

00:15:33.330 --> 00:15:35.000
Wh-Why are <i>you </i>here?

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:37.620
I brought this from
Lady Iko in the capital.

00:15:39.460 --> 00:15:42.250
She was worried about you.

00:15:45.720 --> 00:15:49.180
What're you looking at?
You did your job. Now go!

00:15:53.930 --> 00:15:55.390
Oh, wait!

00:15:55.390 --> 00:15:57.270
I'll write a reply, so--

00:15:57.270 --> 00:15:59.270
I'm staying.

00:15:59.270 --> 00:16:01.360
I'm staying here.

00:16:01.360 --> 00:16:04.030
Do you understand the situation we're in?

00:16:07.450 --> 00:16:08.450
No, no, no--

00:16:08.450 --> 00:16:10.660
I decided to witness it.

00:16:10.660 --> 00:16:14.700
To witness your future, and the Heike's.

00:16:14.700 --> 00:16:20.460
To witness the clan's end
after we got high and mighty?

00:16:20.460 --> 00:16:22.540
I want to pass down the story.

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:25.840
I'm sure I don't even appear in the story.

00:16:25.840 --> 00:16:26.420
You do.

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:27.670
What?

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:34.640
Shigemori, Koremori, You, Kiyotsune,
and Atsumori--all of you do.

00:16:34.640 --> 00:16:39.270
Your first appearance will likely
be the incident with the regent.

00:16:39.270 --> 00:16:43.940
The incident with Lord Motofusa?
I was still a dumb kid then.

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:55.040
I met all of you and knew you.

00:16:55.040 --> 00:16:58.580
So I will just tell what I saw and heard.

00:17:03.670 --> 00:17:06.300
Biwa!

00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:11.890
His name is Neko.

00:17:11.890 --> 00:17:13.090
Neko!

00:17:13.090 --> 00:17:14.760
Emperor.

00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:16.510
Biwa, it's so good to--

00:17:16.510 --> 00:17:18.220
Tokuko.

00:17:18.220 --> 00:17:19.810
I saw my Ma.

00:17:19.810 --> 00:17:23.520
You did? I'm glad for you.

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:27.360
She never stopped worrying about me.

00:17:27.360 --> 00:17:28.360
I see.

00:17:30.570 --> 00:17:33.780
That's what it means
to be a mother, right?

00:17:38.660 --> 00:17:41.710
Wait! Be my pet cat!

00:17:41.710 --> 00:17:46.420
I'm afraid that can't be.
A local fisherman will take Neko.

00:17:49.630 --> 00:17:55.640
The Genji army has headed west
with Lord Noriyori in command.

00:17:55.640 --> 00:18:01.770
At a loss about how to proceed, Lord
Noriyori has retreated to Aki province.

00:18:01.770 --> 00:18:04.900
My, the Heike are so stubborn.

00:18:04.900 --> 00:18:09.280
Tomomori of the Taira is
a capable commander...

00:18:09.280 --> 00:18:11.950
Should I... send Yoshitsune?

00:18:16.240 --> 00:18:18.620
Shizuka, are you not hungry?

00:18:18.620 --> 00:18:21.580
She's worried about Lord Yoshitsune.

00:18:21.580 --> 00:18:26.250
It must be nice, to have the affections
of the Genji commander!

00:18:32.090 --> 00:18:37.010
It'll be fine. Lord Yoshitsune has
a reputation for skilled battle.

00:18:44.770 --> 00:18:47.480
The Genji army is attacking!

00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:58.280
They crossed the sea
on the night of a storm?!

00:18:58.280 --> 00:19:00.120
There are stars flying all over!

00:19:00.120 --> 00:19:01.120
Emperor.

00:19:03.540 --> 00:19:04.540
Fire!

00:19:05.500 --> 00:19:10.460
Lord Yoshitsune has at last driven
the Heike from Yashima toward the sea.

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:12.510
Splendid work.

00:19:12.510 --> 00:19:17.140
I hear the Heike continued out to sea,
but Yoshitsune's warriors...

00:19:17.140 --> 00:19:19.180
They number only 70 riders?

00:19:19.180 --> 00:19:21.470
And so the Heike turned back.

00:19:21.470 --> 00:19:26.690
However, Yoshitsune drove them
back out to sea once more.

00:19:26.690 --> 00:19:30.980
In a fit of rage, the Heike
challenged the Genji to hit a fan.

00:19:33.990 --> 00:19:36.280
A man known as Nasu no Yoichi...

00:19:39.410 --> 00:19:42.950
...fired an arrow straight
into that target.

00:19:47.040 --> 00:19:53.300
Seizing the momentum, Lord Yoshitsune
subdued the Heike's fragmented forces.

00:19:54.590 --> 00:19:59.550
Now they should finally
return the Sacred Treasures.

00:19:59.550 --> 00:20:01.510
I shall send a letter, and--

00:20:01.510 --> 00:20:03.140
I'm afraid that...

00:20:03.140 --> 00:20:06.350
Eliminate the flowers, the buds,
even the seeds.

00:20:07.940 --> 00:20:12.270
...the Genji mean to choke the life
out of the Heike and end them.

00:20:12.270 --> 00:20:14.730
They have sailed for Dannoura.

00:20:42.390 --> 00:20:45.890
♪ The Heike boats numbered 1,000. ♪

00:20:45.890 --> 00:20:49.140
♪ The Genji boats numbered 3,000. ♪

00:20:50.480 --> 00:20:56.820
♪ The two forces faced each other
and shouted their battle cries. ♪

00:20:56.820 --> 00:21:03.200
♪ The cries were thought to
have reached Brahma above ♪

00:21:03.200 --> 00:21:07.200
♪ and startled the Dragon Sea God below. ♪

00:21:12.790 --> 00:21:15.000
Today is the final battle!

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:17.590
Do not let your hearts retreat!

00:21:17.590 --> 00:21:19.340
Value not your lives!

00:21:19.340 --> 00:21:21.800
Value your renown!
